$q$, 'PREDICT_OUTPUT', $o$["outer / inner", "outer then a deadlock", "inner / outer", "IllegalMonitorStateException"]$o$, 'outer / inner', $e$Java monitors are reentrant: the thread that owns a lock can enter another synchronized block on it.$e$, 10, 3, now(), now()),
    ('a77ac6da-74c2-5e83-b4c1-af155976dde3', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000004', $q$A consumer must wait until a queue is non-empty. Which pattern is correct with wait()/notify()?$q$, 'CHOOSE_APPROACH', $o$["while (queue.isEmpty()) wait();", "if (queue.isEmpty()) wait();", "Thread.sleep(10) in a loop outside synchronized", "Call notify() before wait()"]$o$, 'while (queue.isEmpty()) wait();', $e$Always re-check the condition in a loop: wakeups can be spurious or the condition may be consumed by another thread first.$e$, 10, 4, now(), now()),
    ('db44f49e-3854-5d3c-ae11-da24e9e0e686', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000004', $q$What happens if wait() is called by a thread that does not hold the object's monitor?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["IllegalMonitorStateException", "It blocks forever", "It returns immediately", "The monitor is acquired automatically"]$o$, 'IllegalMonitorStateException', $e$wait(), notify() and notifyAll() must be called while holding the monitor of the object.$e$, 10, 5, now(), now()),
    ('caa74e31-c666-5f6d-8837-c6010d217d5e', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000005', $q$Where must lock.unlock() be called after lock.lock()?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["In a finally block", "Only at the end of main", "Right before lock()", "It is optional"]$o$, 'In a finally block', $e$If the guarded code throws, only a finally block guarantees the lock is released.$e$, 10, 1, now(), now()),
    ('ca14bcf3-4453-556a-aa64-8491b20ce021', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000005', $q$What does tryLock() do?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["Returns immediately with true if the lock was acquired, false otherwise", "Blocks until the lock is free", "Throws if the lock is busy", "Always acquires the lock"]$o$, 'Returns immediately with true if the lock was acquired, false otherwise', $e$tryLock() never blocks (the timed variant waits up to a timeout), which makes deadlock avoidance possible.$e$, 10, 2, now(), now()),
    ('e88ddb22-d8a6-55a0-809e-695a324596ac', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000005', $q$What does this program print? (Lines are shown separated by " / ".)

import java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();
        lock.lock();
        lock.lock();
        System.out.println(lock.getHoldCount());
        lock.unlock();
        lock.unlock();
    }
}
$q$, 'PREDICT_OUTPUT', $o$["2", "1", "0", "IllegalMonitorStateException"]$o$, '2', $e$ReentrantLock counts holds per thread: locking twice gives a hold count of 2.$e$, 10, 3, now(), now()),
    ('9c9a4150-21da-515e-a8c6-726d8f911a38', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000005', $q$A cache is read by many threads and updated rarely. Which lock fits best?$q$, 'CHOOSE_APPROACH', $o$["ReentrantReadWriteLock", "synchronized on every method", "A Semaphore with one permit", "Thread.yield()"]$o$, 'ReentrantReadWriteLock', $e$A read-write lock lets many readers proceed in parallel and only blocks them while a writer holds the lock.$e$, 10, 4, now(), now()),
    ('a2cbe819-3a7b-58e3-b221-aac7fed58831', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000005', $q$Which feature does ReentrantLock offer that synchronized does not?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["tryLock, timed and interruptible acquisition, and optional fairness", "Automatic release on exception", "Reentrancy", "Mutual exclusion"]$o$, 'tryLock, timed and interruptible acquisition, and optional fairness', $e$Both are reentrant and mutually exclusive; ReentrantLock adds tryLock, timeouts, interruptible locking and fairness.$e$, 10, 5, now(), now()),
    ('5f18d0b2-b0fd-58b5-8f94-9dc1830e9b0f', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000006', $q$Which of these is NOT one of the four conditions required for a deadlock?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["Preemption (locks can be forcibly taken away)", "Mutual exclusion", "Hold and wait", "Circular wait"]$o$, 'Preemption (locks can be forcibly taken away)', $e$Deadlock needs mutual exclusion, hold and wait, NO preemption, and circular wait. Allowing preemption breaks it.$e$, 10, 1, now(), now()),
    ('ca5f64d7-e85a-56e8-a88c-29e3aef2e30a', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000006', $q$Two methods lock account A then B, and B then A. What is the standard fix?$q$, 'CHOOSE_APPROACH', $o$["Always acquire locks in one global order (for example by account id)", "Add more threads", "Make both locks volatile", "Call Thread.sleep() between the locks"]$o$, 'Always acquire locks in one global order (for example by account id)', $e$A consistent global lock order makes a circular wait impossible.$e$, 10, 2, now(), now()),
    ('ee7ae310-3b55-5c4f-95b0-c1a43c380676', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000006', $q$Thread A holds L1 and waits for L2 while thread B holds L2 and waits for L1. What is this?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["Deadlock", "Livelock", "Starvation", "A race condition"]$o$, 'Deadlock', $e$Both threads block forever waiting for each other: a classic deadlock.$e$, 10, 3, now(), now()),
    ('4cf1de23-93a9-5981-b5da-609b9b7a4f83', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000006', $q$What does this program print? (Lines are shown separated by " / ".)

import java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();
        lock.lock();
        Thread other = new Thread(() -> System.out.println(lock.tryLock()));
        other.start();
        other.join();
        lock.unlock();
    }
}
$q$, 'PREDICT_OUTPUT', $o$["false", "true", "It deadlocks", "IllegalMonitorStateException"]$o$, 'false', $e$The main thread owns the lock, so tryLock() from another thread fails immediately instead of blocking.$e$, 10, 4, now(), now()),
    ('0a12db36-a08f-5cdc-987c-66045ef5c23a', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000006', $q$Which tool can show you a deadlock in a running JVM?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["A thread dump (for example jstack)", "javac", "javadoc", "jar"]$o$, 'A thread dump (for example jstack)', $e$Thread dumps list which thread owns which monitor and report detected Java-level deadlocks.$e$, 10, 5, now(), now()),
    ('01d2e2fa-ad3a-52f5-b3c6-e3efdcf0f0b7', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000007', $q$Two threads keep changing state in response to each other but neither makes progress. What is this called?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["Livelock", "Deadlock", "Race condition", "Thread confinement"]$o$, 'Livelock', $e$In a livelock threads are active but keep reacting to one another without progress; in a deadlock they are blocked.$e$, 20, 1, now(), now()),
