    ('2ea35a6b-a391-553f-811b-49f517ce8f8e', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000007', $q$Lazy singleton initialization is called from many threads. Which is the safest simple approach?$q$, 'CHOOSE_APPROACH', $o$["The initialization-on-demand holder idiom (static nested class)", "A plain if (instance == null) check", "A non-volatile double-checked lock", "Catching the exception and retrying"]$o$, 'The initialization-on-demand holder idiom (static nested class)', $e$Class initialization is guaranteed thread-safe by the JVM, and the holder class loads lazily on first use.$e$, 20, 3, now(), now()),
    ('03ff8990-afa3-56d1-9669-f26772a2145d', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000007', $q$What does this program print? (Lines are shown separated by " / ".)

public class Main {
    static class Counter {
        private int n = 0;

        synchronized void inc() {
            n++;
        }

        int get() {
            return n;
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Counter c = new Counter();
        Thread[] ts = new Thread[4];
        for (int i = 0; i < ts.length; i++) {
            ts[i] = new Thread(() -> {
                for (int j = 0; j < 250; j++) c.inc();
            });
            ts[i].start();
        }
        for (Thread t : ts) t.join();
        System.out.println(c.get());
    }
}
$q$, 'PREDICT_OUTPUT', $o$["1000", "Anything up to 1000", "250", "Compilation error"]$o$, '1000', $e$inc() is synchronized on the shared Counter, so all 4 x 250 increments are applied. (get() is only called after join.)$e$, 20, 4, now(), now()),
    ('faab8d53-0eab-54ec-9cfb-ee4e55f1b8d2', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000007', $q$Which fix is best when many threads wait for a long time on one lock held by a slow thread?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["Use tryLock with a timeout and back off", "Add more threads", "Declare the shared field volatile", "Call wait() in a loop without a lock"]$o$, 'Use tryLock with a timeout and back off', $e$A timed tryLock lets a thread give up, release what it holds and retry, instead of blocking indefinitely.$e$, 20, 5, now(), now()),
    ('ae258806-06ad-5ffe-bbf4-9a0204415e62', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000007', $q$Why must a condition be re-checked in a while loop around wait()?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["Spurious wakeups and competing consumers can make the condition false again", "Because wait() is slow", "Because notify() is not thread-safe", "Because loops are required by the compiler"]$o$, 'Spurious wakeups and competing consumers can make the condition false again', $e$A woken thread must re-test the condition because another thread may have changed the state before it re-acquired the monitor.$e$, 20, 6, now(), now()),
    ('2ef8d578-7c7b-5d7b-a0e6-b46ad4f3f347', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000007', $q$Which strategy prevents the circular wait in a dining-philosophers style program?$q$, 'CHOOSE_APPROACH', $o$["Number the resources and always pick up the lower-numbered one first", "Let every philosopher grab the left fork first", "Use more forks than philosophers but no ordering", "Sleep a random time and retry"]$o$, 'Number the resources and always pick up the lower-numbered one first', $e$Resource ordering removes the circular-wait condition, so deadlock cannot occur.$e$, 20, 7, now(), now()),
    ('b2efdeba-e966-5b54-8bf7-f706f70f7afb', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000b000007', $q$A ReentrantLock is locked twice by the same thread. How many unlock() calls release it fully?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["2", "1", "0", "It depends on the JVM"]$o$, '2', $e$Each lock() increments the hold count; the lock is released only when the count returns to zero.$e$, 20, 8, now(), now())
